// key-switch-rs configuration
//
// Changes are applied when you save: the daemon reloads this file about
// 250 ms after the save, without a restart. If the new version does not
// load, the error is printed and the previous bindings stay active.
// Deleting or renaming this file keeps the current bindings. The daemon
// writes this template only when it starts and finds no config.ron next to
// key-switch-rs.exe; a config path given on the command line must exist.
// Field names are checked: an unknown or misspelled field is an error.
// Save as UTF-8, with or without a BOM.
//
// ---- binding kinds ----
//
// Every binding specifies exactly one of:
//
//   keys:     "<combo>"               — classic press-this-combination
//   sequence: (steps: [...], ...)     — Vim/Emacs-style ordered sequence
//   chord:    (keys: [...], ...)      — simultaneous chord (F13+F14 together)
//
// max_gap_ms (default 500) and window_ms (default 50) are 1 to 10000 ms.
//
// Examples:
//
//   ( keys: "Ctrl+Alt+L", action: PressKey("L") )
//
//   ( sequence: (steps: ["F13", "F14"], max_gap_ms: 500),
//     action: PressKey("Home") )                 // press F13, then F14
//
//   ( chord: (keys: ["F13", "F14"], window_ms: 50),
//     action: PressKey("Escape") )               // press F13 and F14 together
//
// CAVEAT — Sequence/Chord eat their trigger keys: if a sequence fails to
// complete (timeout or wrong next key) the suppressed key-downs are lost,
// not replayed. Bind sequences/chords to keys you don't use in normal typing.
//
// ---- combo syntax (the `keys` field) ----
//
// "+"-joined list. Whitespace around segments is ignored and matching is
// case-insensitive.
//
//   Modifiers : Shift, Ctrl/Control, Alt/Menu, Win/Super match either key
//               of the pair; LShift, RShift, LCtrl, RCtrl, LAlt, RAlt,
//               LWin, RWin (also LeftShift, RightWin, ...) match only that
//               key. The same holds for sequence steps and chord keys.
//   Letters   : A-Z
//   Digits    : 0-9
//   Function  : F1..F24
//   Numpad    : Num0..Num9 (or Numpad0..Numpad9)
//   Named     : CapsLock (Caps), Tab, Esc (Escape), Enter (Return),
//               Space (Spacebar), Backspace (Back), Delete (Del),
//               Insert (Ins), Home, End, PageUp (PgUp), PageDown (PgDn),
//               Up (UpArrow), Down (DownArrow), Left (LeftArrow),
//               Right (RightArrow), NumLock, ScrollLock (Scroll),
//               Pause (Break), PrintScreen (PrtSc, PrtScn)
//   Media     : MediaPlayPause (PlayPause), MediaStop, MediaNext
//               (NextTrack), MediaPrev (MediaPrevious, PrevTrack),
//               VolumeUp (VolUp), VolumeDown (VolDown),
//               VolumeMute (VolMute, Mute)
//   OEM punc  : ` - = , . ; / [ ] \ '
//
// Examples: "CapsLock", "Shift+CapsLock", "Ctrl+Alt+Delete", "Win+L",
//           "Ctrl+Shift+Esc", "F13".
//
// A binding fires (or arms its Tap/Hold/DoubleTap) only on the key-down of
// one of its own keys: a non-modifier key, or any key of a binding made
// only of modifiers ("Alt+Shift", "LShift"). Press the modifiers first:
// Shift, then CapsLock fires "Shift+CapsLock"; CapsLock, then Shift does
// not. Keys typed while CapsLock is held reach the application.
//
// Modifiers match exactly: the modifiers held (Shift, Ctrl, Alt, Win;
// either key of a pair counts) must be the ones the binding names.
// "CapsLock" does not fire while Shift, Ctrl, Alt or Win is held, and
// "Ctrl+J" does not fire on Ctrl+Shift+J. Set allow_extra_modifiers: true
// on a binding to let it fire while other modifiers are held too.
//
// ---- action variants ----
//
// SwitchLanguage          — next keyboard layout
// SwitchLanguageBackward  — previous keyboard layout
// ToggleCapsLock          — toggle CapsLock state
// PressKey("<name>")      — synthesize a key press
// PostMessage(            — PostMessage to foreground window
//     msg: "WM_CLOSE",    //   string name, or a numeric code like 0x10
//     wparam: 0,          //   optional, default 0
//     lparam: 0,          //   optional, default 0
// )
// Launch(                 — spawn a process. Until roadmap item 3.3 it
//                            gets the daemon's administrator rights and,
//                            for a console program, its console.
//     exe: "code.exe",    //   absolute path or PATH name
//     args: ["D:\\proj"], //   optional, default []
// )
// OpenUrl("https://...")  — ShellExecute "open": URL, mailto:, file path, exe
// Media(<key>)            — synthesize media/volume key. <key> is one of:
//                            PlayPause, Stop, Next, Previous,
//                            VolumeUp, VolumeDown, VolumeMute
// Sequence([...])         — chained macro steps (see below)
// DoNothing               — accept and drop the combo
//
// ---- trigger (when the action fires) ----
//
// Each binding has an optional `trigger:` field, defaulting to Immediate:
//
//   trigger: Immediate           — fire on key-down (the default); on an
//                                  auto-repeat only with repeat (see the
//                                  per-binding flags)
//   trigger: Tap(200)            — fire on key-up if released within 200 ms
//   trigger: Hold(200)           — fire after key held for 200 ms
//   trigger: DoubleTap(250)      — fire on second key-down within 250 ms
//                                  of the first
//
// Terms are 1 to 10000 ms.
//
// Multiple bindings on the same combo and when: with different triggers
// coexist: e.g. one Tap(200) binding for SwitchLanguage and one Hold(200)
// binding for PressKey("LShift") on CapsLock arm both gestures on key-down.
// With equal terms exactly one of them fires: Tap if the key is released
// before 200 ms, Hold otherwise. The Hold sends one LShift press at that
// moment, not a held Shift.
//
// One binding wins each key press: of the bindings that match it, the one
// with more keys, then one with a when: over one without, then the one
// higher in this file. Only the winner runs and decides whether the key is
// swallowed; Tap, Hold and DoubleTap bindings on the same keys with the
// same when: win together. An Immediate binding and a Tap or Hold on the
// same keys never act on the same press; with the same when:, the higher
// one wins every press.
//
// Known WM_* names: WM_CLOSE, WM_QUIT, WM_DESTROY, WM_COMMAND,
// WM_SYSCOMMAND, WM_INPUTLANGCHANGEREQUEST, WM_KEYDOWN, WM_KEYUP,
// WM_SYSKEYDOWN, WM_SYSKEYUP, WM_HOTKEY. Anything else: pass a number.
//
// ---- sequence step variants ----
//
// Window(Minimize)        — Minimize | Maximize | Restore | Close
//                            Operates on the window that was foreground
//                            when the binding fired (captured once at the
//                            start of the sequence — subsequent focus
//                            changes don't redirect it).
// Delay(100)              — sleep N ms (worker thread, not the hook)
// Text("Hello 🚀")        — type Unicode (layout-independent, supports
//                            emoji via UTF-16 surrogate pairs)
// Key("Enter")            — synthesize one key press
// Combo("Ctrl+S")         — synthesize a chord (modifiers held during press)
// Launch(exe: "...", args: [...])
//                         - spawn a process (same as the action)
// OpenUrl("...")          - open with the default handler (same as the action)
// Media(<key>)            - synthesize a media key (same as the action)
//
// ---- per-binding flags ----
//
// block_default: true   (default true; false for a Tap, Hold or DoubleTap
//                        binding made only of modifiers, such as "LShift")
//                       - suppress the key's OS events: its press, its
//                         auto-repeats and its release. With false they
//                         reach applications, and a Tap, Hold or DoubleTap
//                         still detects its gesture. Only the binding that
//                         wins a key press counts. sequence and chord
//                         bindings ignore it.
// block_original_combo: true (default false)
//                       — auto-block the OS-default hotkey that normally
//                         triggers this action's underlying function.
//                         Useful when remapping language switching: we set
//                         keys: "CapsLock" but Windows still ships
//                         Alt+Shift / Ctrl+Shift as the language hotkey,
//                         and this flag silences it.
//                         It is not added when a binding in this file
//                         uses the hotkey's keys itself.
//                         It acts only on the hotkey pressed on its own:
//                         Shift pressed while Alt and Tab are held still
//                         reaches Windows.
//                         Until roadmap item 1.2 it ignores the binding's
//                         when: and acts in every window (KS-35).
// allow_extra_modifiers: true (default false)
//                       - keys bindings only: also fire while modifiers
//                         the binding does not name are held. A load
//                         error on sequence and chord bindings.
// repeat: true | false  (default true for PressKey, Media(VolumeUp) and
//                        Media(VolumeDown), false for every other action)
//                       - keys bindings with the Immediate trigger: also fire
//                         on every auto-repeat while the key is held. With
//                         false the action fires once per press; the
//                         repeats are still swallowed when the press was.
//                         repeat: true is a load error on Tap, Hold,
//                         DoubleTap, sequence and chord bindings, which
//                         never fire on an auto-repeat.
//                         Each repeat of a PressKey sends a new press: for
//                         a toggle key (CapsLock, NumLock) or a modifier,
//                         write repeat: false.
//
// ---- conditions (`when:` field) ----
//
// Gate a binding on the focused window. Missing or Always: binding fires
// unconditionally. Variants (string comparisons ignore case, in every alphabet):
//
//   Always
//   AppEquals("code.exe")           — exe base name of focused window
//   TitleContains("Spotify")        — substring of window title
//   TitleEquals("Calculator")       — exact window title
//   Not(<sub>)                      — negation
//   And([<sub1>, <sub2>, ...])      — all must match
//   Or([<sub1>, <sub2>, ...])       — any must match

(
    bindings: [
        (
            keys: "CapsLock",
            action: SwitchLanguage,
            block_original_combo: true,
        ),
        (
            keys: "Shift+CapsLock",
            action: ToggleCapsLock,
        ),

        // ---- examples (uncomment to enable) ----
        //
        // (
        //     keys: "Ctrl+Shift+L",
        //     action: PressKey("L"),
        // ),
        // (
        //     keys: "Win+Q",
        //     action: PostMessage(msg: "WM_CLOSE"),
        // ),
        // (
        //     keys: "F13",
        //     action: SwitchLanguageBackward,
        // ),
        //
        // // Launch a process by hotkey
        // ( keys: "Win+Alt+T", action: Launch(exe: "wt.exe") ),
        // ( keys: "Win+Alt+C",
        //   action: Launch(exe: "code.exe", args: ["D:\\projects"]) ),
        //
        // // Open a URL / file via the OS default handler
        // ( keys: "Win+Alt+G", action: OpenUrl("https://github.com") ),
        // ( keys: "Win+Alt+M", action: OpenUrl("mailto:me@example.com") ),
        //
        // // Media / volume controls. VolumeUp/VolumeDown keep changing the
        // // volume while held; the others fire once per press unless
        // // repeat: true (the last line skips tracks while held):
        // ( keys: "Pause",       action: Media(PlayPause) ),
        // ( keys: "Ctrl+Pause",  action: Media(Next) ),
        // ( keys: "Alt+Up",      action: Media(VolumeUp) ),
        // ( keys: "Alt+Down",    action: Media(VolumeDown) ),
        // ( keys: "Alt+M",       action: Media(VolumeMute) ),
        // ( keys: "Ctrl+Alt+PageDown", action: Media(Next), repeat: true ),
        //
        // // Per-app condition: Pause acts as media play/pause only when
        // // Spotify is foreground.
        // (
        //     keys: "Pause",
        //     action: Media(PlayPause),
        //     when: AppEquals("Spotify.exe"),
        // ),
        //
        // // Per-app condition with complex predicate.
        // (
        //     keys: "Ctrl+Alt+L",
        //     action: PressKey("L"),
        //     when: And([
        //         AppEquals("chrome.exe"),
        //         Not(TitleContains("Incognito")),
        //     ]),
        // ),
        //
        // // Two bindings on the same key — one for quick tap, one for hold.
        // // Both arm on key-down; whichever wins on key-up / timer fires.
        // // Replace the CapsLock binding at the top with these two: a
        // // binding listed first on the same keys wins every press.
        // (
        //     keys: "CapsLock",
        //     action: SwitchLanguage,
        //     trigger: Tap(200),
        //     block_original_combo: true,
        // ),
        // (
        //     keys: "CapsLock",
        //     action: PressKey("LShift"),
        //     trigger: Hold(200),
        // ),
        //
        // // Double-tap LShift to toggle CapsLock state. Made only of
        // // modifiers, it lets every left-Shift press still reach
        // // applications, so the left Shift keeps typing capitals. Pressing
        // // the left Shift twice within 250 ms for two capitals (typing
        // // "<T>") toggles CapsLock too; add block_default: true to keep the
        // // left Shift for the double tap alone.
        // (
        //     keys: "LShift",
        //     action: ToggleCapsLock,
        //     trigger: DoubleTap(250),
        // ),
        //
        // // Sequence (Vim-style): F13, then F13 again within 500ms → fire.
        // // F13 is used here intentionally — don't use letters from normal
        // // typing, or your text will be eaten while sequences match.
        // (
        //     sequence: (steps: ["F13", "F13"], max_gap_ms: 500),
        //     action: PressKey("Home"),
        // ),
        //
        // // Chord (simultaneous): press F13 and F14 within 50ms → fire.
        // (
        //     chord: (keys: ["F13", "F14"], window_ms: 50),
        //     action: PressKey("Escape"),
        // ),
        //
        // // Macro: restore active window, type a note, save (Ctrl+S),
        // // minimize back.
        // (
        //     keys: "Ctrl+Alt+N",
        //     action: Sequence([
        //         Window(Restore),
        //         Delay(100),
        //         Text("Note: groceries 🛒"),
        //         Key("Enter"),
        //         Text("Date: 2026-05-24"),
        //         Combo("Ctrl+S"),
        //         Delay(500),
        //         Window(Minimize),
        //     ]),
        // ),
    ],
)
